<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Ararat</h1><p class="st-meta">1927 CE – 1930 CE · capital Kurd Ava</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kurdish self-proclaimed republic around Mount Ararat, crushed by Turkey in 1930.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the failure of the Sheikh Said rebellion of 1925, Kurdish nationalists founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xoybun">Xoybun</a> league in 1927. That year, in October, it proclaimed a Kurdish republic in the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Mount Ararat</a>, near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ihsan-nuri-pasha">Ihsan Nuri Pasha</a> as military commander and the tribal leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-heski">Ibrahim Heski</a> as civil governor.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was a rebel administration based in the mountain villages, with its centre at Kurd Ava, relying on tribal fighters and support from Kurdish exiles. Its control was limited to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Ararat</a> massif and surrounding valleys.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> launched major campaigns in 1930, accompanied by mass killings in the Zilan valley. Turkish forces, operating close to and across the Iranian border, encircled the rebels, who were defeated by autumn 1930. Turkey and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> adjusted their border in 1932, giving Turkey the slopes of Little <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Ararat</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-ararat.jpg" alt="Republic of Ararat" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Benohight214 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurdish_flag_(Khoiboun).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1927 CE – 1930 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kurd Ava</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ihsan Nuri Pasha, Ibrahim Heski</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kurdish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kurdish Republic of Ararat, Republic of Agri</dd></dl></aside></div>
